# neither 6.7.14's `( .. ).name` statement nor D19's parenthesised destination — and now print what the read `(pn)[0]`
# prints, "a subscript's base is a name, a *T field or a call returning *T - name the pointer first (var q: *T = ..;
# q[i])", once at the `(`, the statement stepped in sync (the latch as it was), so the next statement is parsed
